FerrionOS change to relibc (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 74b5e7e315043a21b599f271d5692727aa54f64d with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied (meant for upstream: yes):
- Parse DT_BIND_NOW, DF_BIND_NOW (DT_FLAGS), and DF_1_NOW (DT_FLAGS_1) in src/ld_so/dso.rs and enforce immediate PLT binding per object in DSO::relocate; skip writing lazy trampoline slots into GOT when jmprel/pltrelsz is empty or binding is immediate.
- Enforce PT_GNU_RELRO with PROT_READ (rounding both start and end down to page boundaries with checked arithmetic) after relocation and PT_LOAD protection in DSO::relocate, including for ld.so (libc.so) itself.
- In static_init (src/ld_so/mod.rs), scan all program headers instead of returning early after PT_TLS, compute load_base from PT_PHDR when present, and protect the static binary's PT_GNU_RELRO range with PROT_READ.
- Link libc.so with -Wl,-z,relro -Wl,-z,now in Makefile.

